objetive: git commit wrapper which uses AI to write nice commit messages and is same
convenience as plain 'git commit' -- AI commit messages are treated as *suggestions*,
can edit, + can easily cancel out of commit through quitting a-la with standard git commit.


- pre-commit hook and AI writing Git commit message should run *in parallel*
  - because *both* hook *and* AI can both take a long time
  - and AI does not change the repo content at all
- if hook finishes with error -> abort AI, quit immediately
- hook output should be shown *including all ANSI codes* i.e. colors etc.

- hook output should be rendered *above* a littel status line that shows progress

  things in [...] are single-character graphics

  example: hook exit code 0 without output in 1.2s; AI commt message gen still running at time 2.3 s

      $ git-commit-ai
      [spinner] 2.3s [1.2s check] pre-commit [hourglass] message

  example: hook emitted stdout / stderr, streamed live as it arrives; both still running:

      $ git-commit-ai
      hook output line 1...
      hook output line 2...
      [spinner] 2.3s [hourglass] pre-commit [hourglass] message

  output after both have finished (and user closed editor):

      $ git-commit-ai
      hook output line 1...
      hook output line 2...
      hook final line
      2.5s [check] pre-commit 1.2s [check] message

  output after failed hook

      $ git-commit-ai
      hook output line 1...
      hook output line 2...
      hook REPORTS ERROR
      2.5s [cross] pre-commit [-] message

  (message gen was aborted)

- pretty colors used - green = success, red = failure

- autogenerated AI prompt cached keyed by prompt content
  (-> prompt content should not include things like current time, so that cache can be reused)

- once pre-commit passes and AI commit message is generated:

  - editor gets opened
  - editor is prepopulated with what looks like Git standard commit message template
    - INCLUDING showing the diff
    - (ideally diffstat at the top)
  - user must have affordance to
      (a) accept AI prompt *in their $EDITOR of choice* (if it's jsut nvim compatible I'm actually OK with that)
          by *just re-saving the initial input they see when editor opens over itself*
          (i.e. how it works with git COMMIT_MSG by default)
      (b) *cancel* the commit by just *quitting without writing* and this *MUST NOT* actually commit
      (c) edit the commit message, write, commit with that message
  - NOTE:
      - write a file -> open editor over that file -> use content of file as commit msg
        => BAD, DOESN'T WORK -- no cancel affordance
      - send the AI commit + git COMMIT_MSG templ. incl. diff as template via standard Git feature
        => BAD, DOESN'T WORK -- because if you just write the same file back, IIUC Git treats that as cancellation
    - open to other solution options
    - we can probably decouple the "run AI commit msg gen in parallel with precommit" from this part --
      pipeline can be 1. (run precommit & generate commit msg) in parallel, 2. once done, do [something] to check with user if use it / edit it / abort
